    {
      "id": "panel-routing-overrides",
      "title": "Adaptive Routing Overrides Over Time",
      "description": "SELF-OBSERVATION: count of scanner/fixer spans carrying a non-empty `routing.override_reason` attribute (set by self_observer.adaptive_select_model via ai_agent._select_model_adaptive whenever telemetry-driven routing downgraded the model), grouped by reason (e.g. 'cost_budget_exceeded: ...', 'conservation_mode_active'). ASSUMPTION: `routing.override_reason` is a span attribute, not a metric — this queries the trace/span data source and filters on attribute existence. If your SigNoz instance's span-attribute indexing excludes this key, add it to the span attribute allow-list before this panel will populate.",
      "panelTypes": "graph",
      "yAxisUnit": "short",
      "query": {
        "queryType": "builder",
        "builder": {
          "queryData": [
            {
              "queryName": "A",
              "expression": "A",
              "legend": "{{routing.override_reason}}",
              "dataSource": "traces",
              "aggregateOperator": "count",
              "timeAggregation": "count",
              "spaceAggregation": "sum",
              "aggregateAttribute": {
                "key": "routing.override_reason",
                "type": "tag",
                "dataType": "string",
                "isColumn": false
              },
              "filters": {
                "op": "AND",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "key": {
                      "key": "routing.override_reason",
                      "type": "tag",
                      "dataType": "string",
                      "isColumn": false
                    },
                    "op": "exists",
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              "groupBy": [
                {
                  "key": "routing.override_reason",
                  "type": "tag",
                  "dataType": "string",
                  "isColumn": false
                }
              ],
              "reduceTo": "sum",
              "disabled": false,
              "stepInterval": 60
            }
          ],
          "queryFormulas": []
        },
        "clickhouse_sql": [
          {
            "name": "A",
            "query": "",
            "legend": "",
            "disabled": false
          }
        ],
        "promql": [
          {
            "name": "A",
            "query": "",
            "legend": "",
            "disabled": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "panel-postmortem-triggers",
      "title": "Postmortem Agent Triggers",
      "description": "SELF-OBSERVATION: recent `circuit_breaker.postmortem` span events (emitted by self_observer.generate_postmortem when a CircuitBreaker transitions to OPEN), showing `breaker.name` and `postmortem.text`, most recent first. ASSUMPTION: SigNoz's trace query builder in this version indexes span EVENT names/attributes the same way as span attributes (queried here via a synthetic `event.name` tag equal to 'circuit_breaker.postmortem'). If span events aren't separately indexed in your SigNoz deployment, this panel needs either (a) the postmortem also written as top-level span attributes on the breaker's own span (not just an event), or (b) a log line emitted alongside the event and this panel repointed at the Logs data source instead of traces.",
      "panelTypes": "table",
      "yAxisUnit": "short",
      "query": {
        "queryType": "builder",
        "builder": {
          "queryData": [
            {
              "queryName": "A",
              "expression": "A",
              "legend": "{{breaker.name}}",
              "dataSource": "traces",
              "aggregateOperator": "noop",
              "timeAggregation": "noop",
              "spaceAggregation": "noop",
              "aggregateAttribute": {
                "key": "postmortem.text",
                "type": "tag",
                "dataType": "string",
                "isColumn": false
              },
              "filters": {
                "op": "AND",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "key": {
                      "key": "event.name",
                      "type": "tag",
                      "dataType": "string",
                      "isColumn": false
                    },
                    "op": "=",
                    "value": "circuit_breaker.postmortem"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "groupBy": [
                {
                  "key": "breaker.name",
                  "type": "tag",
                  "dataType": "string",
                  "isColumn": false
                },
                {
                  "key": "postmortem.text",
                  "type": "tag",
                  "dataType": "string",
                  "isColumn": false
                }
              ],
              "reduceTo": "latest",
              "orderBy": [
                {
                  "columnName": "timestamp",
                  "order": "desc"
                }
              ],
              "limit": 20,
              "disabled": false,
              "stepInterval": 60
            }
          ],
          "queryFormulas": []
        },
        "clickhouse_sql": [
          {
            "name": "A",
            "query": "",
            "legend": "",
            "disabled": false
          }
        ],
        "promql": [
          {
            "name": "A",
            "query": "",
            "legend": "",
            "disabled": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "panel-cost-vs-threshold",
      "title": "Cumulative Cost vs Conservation Threshold",
      "description": "SELF-OBSERVATION: running sum of LLM spend (query A, per-request cost summed over the window) against a static threshold line at $25.00 — CostGuardian's COST_GUARDIAN_CUMULATIVE_THRESHOLD_USD default from self_observer.py (env-configurable; update this threshold value if that env var is overridden in your deployment). ASSUMPTIONS/GAPS: (1) query A sums the existing devguard_llm_cost_per_request histogram over the selected window as a proxy for 'cumulative cost' — this resets with the dashboard's time range rather than tracking a true session-long running total the way CostGuardian does internally, so treat this as directional, not authoritative. For an exact match to CostGuardian's own view, emit a monotonically increasing counter metric (e.g. `devguard_llm_cost_cumulative_usd_total`) from the backend and repoint query A at it. (2) `devguard.conservation_mode_active` (the boolean CostGuardian.is_conservation_mode() flag) is not currently emitted as a metric at all — recommend backend emit it as an OTel gauge (0/1) on each CostGuardian.record_scan() sample so a future overlay/annotation on this panel can show exactly when conservation mode was engaged, rather than inferring it from the cost line crossing the threshold.",
      "panelTypes": "graph",
      "yAxisUnit": "none",
      "thresholds": [
        {
          "index": "conservation-threshold",
          "keyIndex": 0,
          "thresholdValue": 25.0,
          "thresholdUnit": "none",
          "thresholdColor": "#F5222D",
          "thresholdLabel": "Conservation mode threshold ($25.00 default, see COST_GUARDIAN_CUMULATIVE_THRESHOLD_USD)",
          "thresholdOperator": ">",
          "thresholdFormat": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "query": {
        "queryType": "builder",
        "builder": {
          "queryData": [
            {
              "queryName": "A",
              "expression": "A",
              "legend": "cumulative cost (windowed sum, see description)",
              "dataSource": "metrics",
              "aggregateOperator": "sum",
              "timeAggregation": "sum",
              "spaceAggregation": "sum",
              "aggregateAttribute": {
                "key": "devguard.llm.cost_per_request",
                "type": "Histogram",
                "dataType": "float64",
                "isColumn": true
              },
              "filters": {
                "op": "AND",
                "items": []
              },
              "groupBy": [],
              "reduceTo": "sum",
              "disabled": false,
              "stepInterval": 60
            }
          ],
          "queryFormulas": []
        },
        "clickhouse_sql": [
          {
            "name": "A",
